invariant: INV-14
file: cpu_cfg.h
catches: test/host-builds.sh
reason: cpu_cfg.h's x86-64 set loses CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX, so every init refuses
  the value a caller on a CPU with BMI2 and ADX states, and no session runs
  x25519_adx.c (docs/decisions.md 164). test/host-builds.sh reads the header
  for both architectures under the pinned clang and compares each set with
  the bits it writes out.

--- old
     CH_CPU_VAES | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA | CH_CPU_AVX512 |              \
     CH_CPU_BMI2_ADX)
--- new
     CH_CPU_VAES | CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA256 | CH_CPU_AVX512_IFMA | CH_CPU_AVX512)
